WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.240
- Do you sing all the time?

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:02.420
- I can't help it,

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:04.390
but I do want to say something to you.

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:05.930
I brought you a gift.

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:08.960
Because, there is only a few people

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:11.348
that I can re-gift things to.

00:00:11.348 --> 00:00:14.980
And the reason is, is
because we share something,

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:16.665
we share actually many things in common.

00:00:16.665 --> 00:00:17.498
- We do.

00:00:17.498 --> 00:00:18.850
- But I would like for you
to go ahead and open this up.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:20.030
Now, I got two.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:22.806
So, I'm being honest with
you, I'm re-gifting this.

00:00:22.806 --> 00:00:24.176
- Are these best friend necklaces?

00:00:24.176 --> 00:00:25.920
Are we best friends?
- Are we getting married?

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:26.780
(laughter)

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.101
- I'm so in.

00:00:28.101 --> 00:00:29.454
- I think that's gonna happen.

00:00:29.454 --> 00:00:30.650
But anyway, go ahead, and you'll see

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:31.868
why I'm gonna remember--

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:32.701
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:34.757
- Okay, so we have the same initials.

00:00:34.757 --> 00:00:37.520
- I know, I was literally, when
I sent the video memo today

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.353
I was like,

00:00:38.353 --> 00:00:39.186
"From KC to KC."

00:00:39.186 --> 00:00:40.080
I thought it was so clever.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.299
It's not that funny.

00:00:41.299 --> 00:00:43.114
- I got three of these, three!

00:00:43.114 --> 00:00:44.680
- Oh, so you don't need 'em all.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.036
I love it!

00:00:46.036 --> 00:00:47.005
(audience applause)

00:00:47.005 --> 00:00:48.131
Wait, is this for jewelry?

00:00:48.131 --> 00:00:49.134
Or like, what is this?

00:00:49.134 --> 00:00:51.380
- What you do is you put 'em

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.850
on your shoe and just so you know,

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:54.648
Katie Couric got the other one.

00:00:54.648 --> 00:00:56.840
- Oh, there we go, the other KC.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.170
I actually know a lot of
people with our initials.

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:00.011
It's weird.

00:01:00.011 --> 00:01:00.909
(animal noise)

00:01:00.909 --> 00:01:01.742
What in the world?

00:01:01.742 --> 00:01:03.840
It sounded like a gremlin got out.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.503
- It's the kookaburra!

00:01:05.503 --> 00:01:06.600
- It's the kookaburra.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:07.880
I can't say it with a cool accent.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:09.460
- I actually practiced doing him.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.470
- Okay wait, can you harmonize with that?

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:14.320
If we played it, could you
harmonize with the kookaburra?

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.780
Okay, Robert, Bindi--
- Yeah.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:17.940
- Can you bring the bird out?

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:20.204
I'm gonna harmonize with Kristin.

00:01:20.204 --> 00:01:21.269
Come on.

00:01:21.269 --> 00:01:23.423
We're gonna harmonize, we're gonna do it.

00:01:24.652 --> 00:01:25.631
We can do it.

00:01:25.631 --> 00:01:26.464
- This is so exciting.
- Hi, y'all.

00:01:26.464 --> 00:01:28.038
- Good to see you.

00:01:28.038 --> 00:01:29.085
- Look, it's my size.

00:01:29.085 --> 00:01:30.390
(laughter)

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.330
- All right, okay he may
not make a sound now,

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:34.010
Moe won't but hey, can we play it?

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:35.138
We're gonna try--

00:01:35.138 --> 00:01:35.971
this is the sound.

00:01:35.971 --> 00:01:36.804
- This is it, okay.

00:01:36.804 --> 00:01:39.416
(kookaburra call)

00:01:39.416 --> 00:01:43.749
(Kristin mimicking kookaburra call)

00:01:48.526 --> 00:01:49.998
- That was amazing.

00:01:49.998 --> 00:01:51.253
I love you.

00:01:51.253 --> 00:01:53.460
- He doesn't know what to do.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:54.457
This is amazing.

00:01:54.457 --> 00:01:55.290
- This is like most of my boyfriends,

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:56.242
they're scared of me!

00:01:56.242 --> 00:01:59.250
- No literally, you are so great.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.040
- I think he likes you, definitely.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:01.873
That was very good.

00:02:01.873 --> 00:02:03.115
- I thought I got that (mimics kookaburra)

00:02:03.115 --> 00:02:04.444
but not that (mimics kookaburra).

00:02:04.444 --> 00:02:08.340
- You are truly one of
those people that just

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.850
lights up the room, like
every room you walk in,

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:13.600
and I feel like we're
similar in the sense that

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.680
we're both kind of like
bubbly all the time,

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:18.020
but are you always like that?

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:18.853
- No.

00:02:18.853 --> 00:02:20.100
No, I think it's--

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.514
and I think it's important to say this.

00:02:22.514 --> 00:02:25.960
People think, there's
a conception about me,

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:26.793
and probably you too

00:02:26.793 --> 00:02:30.300
that it's rainbows, and unicorns,
and glitter all the time.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.090
But I'm human and I've struggled with

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:34.920
sadness and even--

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:35.890
- I've suffered from depression.

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:37.370
- Depression.

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:39.427
And people are like,

00:02:39.427 --> 00:02:40.397
"Really?

00:02:40.397 --> 00:02:41.280
"That can't be real,"

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:42.380
but I do

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:44.670
and I have tools that help me.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.160
First of all, I have counseling.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.930
I have a great mom that I talk to

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:50.550
and I have a great group
of core girlfriends

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.130
that really listen.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:53.540
And I think that's--

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:56.480
and I have faith and for whatever faith is

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:57.313
for everybody else.

00:02:57.313 --> 00:02:59.340
Mine's God so that helps.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:02.120
What else is confusing, it
can happen from sometimes

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.230
left field and it can be
a small thing that kinda

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.063
makes me go,

00:03:05.063 --> 00:03:05.896
"I'm sad,"

00:03:05.896 --> 00:03:07.830
and you pull yourself out of it.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.020
You put your big girl panties up.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:14.150
Or you take the time, and
be sad, and move through it.

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:15.420
- I think you have to do that.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.657
I think that you do, I'm clapping.

00:03:17.657 --> 00:03:19.163
I also wanted to talk to you though,

00:03:19.163 --> 00:03:21.030
because I know you're dating.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:21.863
- Yes.

00:03:21.863 --> 00:03:23.600
- You're dating so lie,
are you getting married

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:25.309
and do you wanna tell us now?

00:03:25.309 --> 00:03:26.142
I'm just kidding.

00:03:26.142 --> 00:03:27.831
- Girl talk.

00:03:27.831 --> 00:03:28.857
You know what?

00:03:28.857 --> 00:03:31.380
Not to get weird, but I think that also

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:33.500
it's important to say this, especially to

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:36.830
our younger fans and younger
generations of women.

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:39.020
I come from the Bible Belt in Oklahoma,

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:41.857
very proudly so, but with that means

00:03:41.857 --> 00:03:43.550
that you're supposed to get married,

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:45.885
have two point five kids,
and live in the picket...

00:03:45.885 --> 00:03:47.800
You know, white picket fence house.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:49.960
And I didn't choose that for my life,

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:51.150
I had other goals

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:53.980
and at first, it was always a shame, like,

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.890
I shouldn't tell people
that maybe I'm not sure

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:58.250
about having children or even maybe

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.300
getting married, and I've
had great men in my life.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.020
I've got a great one right now.

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:04.360
Marriage might be the deal, it might,

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.470
but it's never what's been my...

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:09.610
It hasn't been what's
defined me or driven me.

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:11.720
And for a long time, I
was shameful about it.

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:14.450
- Yeah, especially from where we're from.

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:15.930
- Because of where we're from.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:17.050
And also,

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:18.390
thank you.

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:20.270
- Did people always think you were gay?

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:21.850
People thought I was gay forever.

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:23.260
- I've had some boyfriends to make me

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:24.594
wish I was gay, but no.

00:04:24.594 --> 00:04:25.708
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:25.708 --> 00:04:27.245
- Me too!

00:04:27.245 --> 00:04:28.078
Me too.

00:04:28.078 --> 00:04:28.911
- No, I'm not.

00:04:28.911 --> 00:04:30.517
And as far as, like people will go,

00:04:30.517 --> 00:04:31.590
"You're not gonna have a child?"

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:33.830
And it's almost like, oh selfish.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:35.250
But I take care of a lot of kids.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:39.150
I have many cousins, I have
Godchildren I take care of,

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:40.970
and this is also important to say,

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:44.200
as an adopted child, if I ever wanna--

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:47.697
if I had that so desire one
day and I wake up and I say,

00:04:47.697 --> 00:04:50.878
"Maybe I missed the boat
or maybe I wanna do that,"

00:04:50.878 --> 00:04:53.500
there's been so many
great examples of women

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:57.340
who've done that and I
would just adopt a child.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:58.915
There's many out there.

00:04:58.915 --> 00:05:03.380
- The thing about that two
is one, that you're picked.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:05.136
Like my mom just got stuck with me.

00:05:05.136 --> 00:05:05.969
(Kristin laughs)

00:05:05.969 --> 00:05:06.802
Like, you were picked.

00:05:06.802 --> 00:05:07.635
Like they got

00:05:07.635 --> 00:05:08.468
to pick you.
- They do say you're chosen.

00:05:08.468 --> 00:05:09.930
- Yeah, that's like really cool.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:11.610
- It's a special feeling
and I've always known

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:12.720
about my adoption.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:15.080
And you know, my family,
they're all chemical engineers,

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.468
and real tall, and you
know, they don't sing

00:05:17.468 --> 00:05:20.690
and thy should never sing, actually ever.

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:21.830
But I don't do math.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:23.550
But we learn from each other, you know?

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:24.440
- That's awesome.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:25.547
That's so great.

00:05:25.547 --> 00:05:27.160
All right, well tell
us about your new album

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:28.200
because I want it?

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.310
- Well it's called "For The Girls."

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:31.710
I made a record for the
girls, by the girls,

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:33.790
all the women that have inspired me.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:36.150
You know, we're talking
Lesley Gore, Judy Garland,

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:37.882
Barbara Streisand, we're
talking Eva Cassidy.

00:05:37.882 --> 00:05:38.750
- Love.

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:40.410
- We're talking a lot of the greats.

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:42.640
And I did it my way but I paid--

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:44.586
I tipped my hats to the greats.

00:05:44.586 --> 00:05:46.940
'Cause "I'm a Woman,"
I asked Jennifer Hudson

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:48.480
and Reba to sing it with me.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:51.130
And then I did "I Will
Always Love You" with Dolly,

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:51.963
which I can't believe--

00:05:51.963 --> 00:05:53.870
- Gosh, that is insane.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:56.610
- My extensions fell out of my head

00:05:56.610 --> 00:05:58.744
when she said yes.

00:05:58.744 --> 00:06:00.350
- She's the loveliest human ever.

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:01.510
That's the best compliment ever.

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:04.896
- Has anyone ever met anyone
that doesn't like Dolly Parton?

00:06:04.896 --> 00:06:07.440
- She's the nicest human in the world.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:08.522
- The nicest!

00:06:08.522 --> 00:06:10.215
(audience applause)

00:06:10.215 --> 00:06:11.369
- And you also,

00:06:11.369 --> 00:06:12.872
this is what I find interesting,

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:16.400
you have a duet with
Ariana but you've known her

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:17.460
since she was little, right?

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:19.540
- Since she was seven
years old, Ariana Grande.

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:20.373
She came--

00:06:20.373 --> 00:06:22.390
there we are, we did
"Hairspray Live" together.

00:06:22.390 --> 00:06:23.590
I love that child.

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:25.450
She came back to see "Wicked,"
her grandma brought her

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:26.283
and she said,

00:06:26.283 --> 00:06:28.101
"My granddaughter wants to sing,"

00:06:28.101 --> 00:06:28.934
and I said,

00:06:28.934 --> 00:06:29.847
"Oh well that's sweet," you know,

00:06:29.847 --> 00:06:30.915
"good luck."

00:06:30.915 --> 00:06:32.440
(laughter)

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:33.290
And then she--

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:34.123
- Worldwide superstar.

00:06:34.123 --> 00:06:34.956
- Yeah, so I'm like,

00:06:34.956 --> 00:06:35.789
"Okay, we'll see."

00:06:35.789 --> 00:06:37.970
And then she kinda sang
something and I was like,

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:40.840
oh, I checked myself
because she was really good.

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:41.673
And I said,

00:06:41.673 --> 00:06:42.620
"Here's a little wand,"

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:44.517
because I created the
role of Glenda and I said,

00:06:44.517 --> 00:06:46.630
"Keep that with you and
have that with you,"

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:48.750
and she kept it all these
years, we've stayed close,

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:50.557
and I wanted to bring...

00:06:50.557 --> 00:06:52.490
I wanted to bring her in the record

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:55.090
and we did "You Don't Own
Me," Lesley Gore's tune.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.570
And it's, I'm so proud of her.

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:58.403
I love her.

00:06:58.403 --> 00:06:59.445
- Oh my God, that's so cool.

00:06:59.445 --> 00:07:00.278
That's so cool.

00:07:00.278 --> 00:07:01.930
- Thank you.

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:02.890
- It's super, super great.

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:05.220
So when are you taking
the album to Broadway?

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:06.053
When can people see it?

00:07:06.053 --> 00:07:07.737
It's in November, right?

00:07:07.737 --> 00:07:08.590
- Yeah, the first two weekends in November

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:10.660
I'll be playing on Broadway
with "For The Girls"

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:12.940
and have very special guests come.

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:14.790
And it's at the Nederlander
Theater and you can

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:16.280
get tickets now and please come see it.

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:17.610
- Oh my God, it's gonna be great.

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:18.450
Here's the funny thing though.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:20.257
We both have like, Broadway in common

00:07:20.257 --> 00:07:21.290
'cause we both grew--

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:24.020
well, you have like actual Broadway.

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:26.270
And then I just grew
up in musical theater.

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:28.444
It's very different.

00:07:28.444 --> 00:07:31.220
But my point is is I remember
my very first musical

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:33.207
when I was a little kid, I was like,

00:07:33.207 --> 00:07:34.040
"Oh, we're--

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:36.127
"Okay, so we're just
gonna break out in song,

00:07:36.127 --> 00:07:38.177
"like we were just talking
and then we're just gonna

00:07:38.177 --> 00:07:39.892
"break out in song, and
then we're gonna go back--"

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:41.170
- Yeah, we call that a Monday on Broadway.

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:42.530
- I know, but it's so awkward.

00:07:42.530 --> 00:07:44.120
It's a beautiful thing but I was like,

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:46.068
how awkward is that that you just like

00:07:46.068 --> 00:07:48.386
go all the sudden in song--

00:07:48.386 --> 00:07:51.106
♪ How can it be ♪

00:07:51.106 --> 00:07:56.106
♪ I feel like I have known her forever ♪

00:07:56.447 --> 00:08:00.850
♪ Could she be my less talented ♪

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:04.070
♪ And long lost sister ♪

00:08:04.070 --> 00:08:06.510
- Oh my gosh, so like
the crazy thing, though,

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:09.908
about this is now you're
in a movie with Scott Wolf

00:08:09.908 --> 00:08:11.572
and you're doing the Hallmark thing?

00:08:11.572 --> 00:08:12.405
- Yes.

00:08:12.405 --> 00:08:13.520
- I love Hallmark Christmas movies.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:15.240
- Oh my God, it's a good movie,

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:17.100
Scott Wolf's in it and
his dreamy, blue eyes.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.150
And I wrote the title song for it.

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:18.983
You'll love it.

00:08:18.983 --> 00:08:19.947
- [Kelly] What's the title song called?

00:08:19.947 --> 00:08:21.550
- "A Christmas Story," Hallmark, watch it.

00:08:21.550 --> 00:08:23.654
- Oh my God, that's so great.

00:08:23.654 --> 00:08:26.738
♪ It all makes sense ♪

00:08:26.738 --> 00:08:29.760
♪ I'll never be alone now ♪

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:31.981
♪ It all ♪

00:08:31.981 --> 00:08:33.464
♪ Makes sense ♪

00:08:33.464 --> 00:08:37.798
♪ She'll always be right here ♪

00:08:37.798 --> 00:08:39.236
(audience cheering)

00:08:39.236 --> 00:08:42.080
- Oh my gosh, so tell me about
the tabernacle choir thing,

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:43.330
that's crazy.

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:44.290
So you sing with them.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:46.090
- The tabernacle choir's
a rite of passage--

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:47.280
you need to do it, girl.

